.\" Manual page for the Bomvakt agent. View it in place with: man ./bomvakt.1
.TH BOMVAKT 1 "2026-11-23" "bomvakt 0.5.4" "Bomvakt"
.SH NAME
bomvakt \- send a web server's access logs to Bomvakt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bomvakt
.RB [ \-\-conf
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-key\-file
.IR file ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B bomvakt \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bomvakt
follows the web server's access logs (nginx or Apache) and sends every line
to Bomvakt, where the account at
.I https://bomvakt.com/konto
shows who hits the server, bots that never run JavaScript included, and
which addresses to ban.
.PP
The agent runs as the systemd service
.BR bomvakt ,
which only reads the logs and sends them. Commands that use the key or change files
(\fBsetup\fR, \fBadd\-domain\fR, \fBpassword\fR, \fBlogs\fR, \fBupdate\fR) need root.
Nothing is changed without showing it and asking first.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Create an account, or join an existing one with its key
.RI ( bv_ ...),
and choose which website this server's log belongs to. Saves the key in
.I /etc/bomvakt/key
and the domain in the config, uses the Apache log when the server has no
nginx, prints the tracking code for the site, and offers to give each
website its own log.
.TP
.BI add\-domain " domain " "\fR[\fB\-\-name \fItext\fR]"
Add a domain or IP address to the account, print its tracking code, and
offer to run
.B bomvakt logs
so the agent reads a log of its own for it. Until then the agent sends
nothing for the new site.
.TP
.BI name " domain " "\fR[\fItext\fR]"
Set the name a site is shown with in the account. No text sets it back to
the domain.
.TP
.B password
Set the password for the web login at bomvakt.com/konto. The key on this
server proves the account is yours, so this also works without an email
address. Can turn two-step login off when the phone is lost. Logs out
every web session of the account.
.TP
.B status
Version, account, domains, each log with its domain and whether it can be
read, websites that share a log or have one the agent does not follow,
the service's last send, and what the rules job last did.
.TP
.B logs
Give each website on the server its own access log, the way certbot edits
a config: finds the nginx server blocks and Apache VirtualHosts, shows
the change as a diff, asks, backs up to
.IR /var/lib/bomvakt/backup ,
edits (lines marked
.I # bomvakt\-added
and
.IR "# bomvakt\-off:" ),
tests the config, rolls back on a failed test, reloads the web server,
and adds the logs under
.B [logs]
in the config. Skips files written by control panels and other tools.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Only show what would change.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Do not ask; take every website.
.TP
.B \-\-undo
Take every change out again.
.RE
.TP
.B rules
Fetch the rules made at bomvakt.com/konto/regler for this server's domains
and apply the ones this agent supports. So far: nginx rate limits, written to
.I /etc/nginx/conf.d/bomvakt\-rate.conf
(http level; nothing goes in the server blocks), tested with
.BR "nginx \-t" ,
put back as they were if the test fails, then nginx is reloaded. Never
touches a file it did not write. And robots.txt, written to the path set on
the domain's Robots.txt tab at bomvakt.com (never through a link; the file
that was there first is copied to
.IR /var/lib/bomvakt\-rules/robots\-backup ).
The timer
.B bomvakt\-rules.timer
runs it every 5 minutes.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Only show what would change.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Fetch and compare even if the server says nothing changed.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print only changes and errors (what the timer uses).
.RE
.TP
.B update
Download the newest installer and run it, so changes to the installer apply at once
(the installed copy is used if the download fails). Keeps the config and the key.
.TP
.BI parse " file"
Show how the lines of a log file are read: the first lines as they would
be sent, and how many could not be read. Sends nothing.
.TP
.B run
Follow the logs and send them. This is what the service runs; it is not
needed by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-conf " file"
The config file. Default:
.IR /etc/bomvakt/bomvakt.conf .
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-file " file"
The file holding the account key. Default:
.IR /etc/bomvakt/key .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I /etc/bomvakt/bomvakt.conf
is an INI file. After a change: \fBsudo systemctl restart bomvakt\fR.
.TP
.B [bomvakt]
.RS
.TP
.B domain
The website the logs under
.B logs
belong to. Set by
.BR setup .
.TP
.B logs
Access logs to follow, comma\-separated. Their lines are sent as
.BR domain .
Default
.IR /var/log/nginx/access.log ;
on a server with Apache and no nginx the agent uses the Apache log
instead and saves that here.
.TP
.B interval
Seconds between summaries in the journal (at least 10). Default 300.
.TP
.B server
Where to send. Leave as is.
.TP
.B rules
.B on
(default) or
.BR off :
whether
.B bomvakt rules
applies the rules from the website.
.RE
.TP
.B [logs]
One line per website with a log of its own,
.IR "path " = " domain" :
.PP
.RS
.nf
[logs]
/var/log/nginx/shop.example.com.access.log = shop.example.com
/var/log/apache2/blog.example.com.access.log = blog.example.com
.fi
.RE
.PP
Every domain has to be on the account first
.RB ( add\-domain );
lines for a domain that is not are dropped by the server.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/bomvakt/bomvakt.py
The agent.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/bomvakt/install.sh
The installer, used for uninstalling and by \fBupdate\fR when the newest one cannot be downloaded.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/bomvakt
Link to the agent.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/bomvakt.service
The service.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/bomvakt\-rules.timer
Runs
.B bomvakt rules
as root every 5 minutes (via
.IR bomvakt\-rules.service ).
.TP
.I /etc/nginx/conf.d/bomvakt\-rate.conf
The nginx rate limits, written by
.BR rules .
Removed by uninstall.
.TP
.I /etc/bomvakt/bomvakt.conf
The config. Kept by uninstall.
.TP
.I /etc/bomvakt/key
The account key, readable by root only. Kept by uninstall. Anyone with the
key can send logs to the account and set its web password: keep a copy
somewhere safe, and never share it.
.TP
.I /var/lib/bomvakt
State: how far each log has been read, lines waiting to be sent, and
backups made by \fBlogs\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BOMVAKT_SERVER
Send to this server instead of the one in the config (testing).
.SH EXAMPLES
Install and set up:
.PP
.RS
.nf
curl \-fsSL https://bomvakt.com/install.sh | sudo sh
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add another website on the same server and give it its own log:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo bomvakt add\-domain shop.example.com \-\-name "Webshop"
sudo bomvakt logs \-\-dry\-run
sudo bomvakt logs
.fi
.RE
.PP
See what the agent does:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo bomvakt status
journalctl \-u bomvakt \-f
.fi
.RE
.PP
Uninstall (keeps config and key), or remove everything:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo /usr/lib/bomvakt/install.sh uninstall
sudo /usr/lib/bomvakt/install.sh purge
.fi
.RE
.SH PRIVACY
The agent sends each log line as the web server wrote it: time, IP address,
request with query string, status, size, referrer and user agent. Bomvakt
keeps the lines for 30 days, for the account only, to decide what to ban.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR nginx (8),
.BR apache2ctl (8),
.BR fail2ban\-client (1),
.BR ipset (8),
.BR ufw (8)
.PP
.I https://bomvakt.com
and
.I https://github.com/torvanger/bomvakt\-linux
.SH AUTHOR
Torvanger AB.
